                <pb facs="0538" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg480"/>

                <head>United States of Colombia, sovereign state of Bolivar–Number 43–The governor
                    of the province of Mangangue.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Magangue</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1864-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 3,
                        1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I return to you, signed, the official note which by an oversight, involuntary, on
                    my part, I left without my signature. I thus answer your note No. 243, section
                    of government, dated April last, 26th.</p>
                <p>I am your attentive servant,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">ANDRES GUTIERREZ.</p>
                <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary General of State, Cartagena</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">May</hi> 14.—Let this be filed.</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">March</hi> 10, 1865.</p>
                <p>A copy:</p>
                <p rendition="#right">M AMADOR FIERRO, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary General of
                        State</hi>.</p>
                <p>A copy:</p>
                <p rendition="#right">ENSPR. DE LA TORRE, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                        Secretary</hi>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
